# Map VeeR's clock gate onto ASAP7's integrated clock gate.
#
# Runs through SYNTH_POST_HIERARCHY_SCRIPTS (patches/0068), which is
# after hierarchy and before flatten -- the only window in which a
# clockhdr instance is still a cell of its own type.
#
# chtype first, because the slang frontend elaborates one module per
# instance and names each after the instance path:
#
#   \clockhdr$swerv_wrapper.mem.free_cg.rvclkhdr
#   \clockhdr$swerv_wrapper.dbg.dbg_free_cg.rvclkhdr
#   ... ~100 more
#
# so there is no cell of type `clockhdr` for techmap to match, and a
# bare techmap -map silently maps nothing -- which is exactly what it
# did: ICG 0, transparent latches 952. chtype folds the uniquified
# copies back onto the one name the map file defines.
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
chtype -set clockhdr t:clockhdr$*
techmap -map test/coremark_joule/flow/cmj_veer_icg_map.v
